      ":question/problem": "![](images/ef/ef5f0bea75f8a29a0d10fe162abd96c73dd98a0d815abf3d231cc4e4450c8eff.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a rational function. It has no vertical asymptotes, and its $x$-intercepts are $(1, 0)$ and $(2, 0)$. Which of the following could be the equation of the graph?\n\n1. $y = ((x - 1)(x - 2))/(4(x^{2} + 1))$\n2. $y = (x^{2} + 2)/(4(x^{2} + 1))$\n3. $y = ((x - 1)(x - 2))/(4(x + 1))$\n\n*(Note: Figure not drawn to scale)*"
